      "side": 1,
      "message": "`std::from_chars` does not automatically ignore `0x` or `0X` prefixes. If a user passes standard hex notation (e.g., `-V 0x04F3`), the parser will fail and exit.\n\n* **Action:** Update `ParseHex` in `util/elan/iap_tool.cc` to strip the prefix before parsing:\n\n```c\nstd::optional\u003cuint16_t\u003e ParseHex(std::string_view strv)\n{\n\tif (strv.empty()) return std::nullopt;\n\n\t// Strip standard hex prefixes\n\tif (strv.starts_with(\"0x\") || strv.starts_with(\"0X\")) {\n\t\tstrv.remove_prefix(2);\n\t}\n\n\tuint16_t val;\n\tauto [ptr, ec] \u003d std::from_chars(\n\t\tstrv.data(), strv.data() + strv.size(), val, 16);\n\n\tif (ec \u003d\u003d std::errc() \u0026\u0026 ptr \u003d\u003d strv.data() + strv.size()) {\n\t\treturn val;\n\t}\n\treturn std::nullopt;\n}\n\n```",
