      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, `LogInfo` handles both standard operational updates and critical failures. It is best practice in CLI utilities to route errors to standard error so users can cleanly pipe output.\n\n* **Action:** In `util/elan/utility.h`, leverage the C++23 `std::print` stream overload to add a `LogErr` function:\n\n```c\n#include \u003ccstdio\u003e\n#include \u003cprint\u003e\n#include \u003cutility\u003e\n\ntemplate \u003ctypename... Args\u003e\nvoid LogInfo(std::format_string\u003cArgs...\u003e fmt, Args \u0026\u0026...args)\n{\n\tstd::print(stdout, fmt, std::forward\u003cArgs\u003e(args)...);\n}\n\ntemplate \u003ctypename... Args\u003e\nvoid LogErr(std::format_string\u003cArgs...\u003e fmt, Args \u0026\u0026...args)\n{\n\tstd::print(stderr, fmt, std::forward\u003cArgs\u003e(args)...);\n}\n\n```\n\n* **Action:** Go through `iap_control.cc` and `iap_tool.cc` and swap `LogInfo` to `LogErr` for all error/failure cases.",
